{# ============================================================================
   HYPER · الفوتر  (footer)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
     │ 💬 خدمة العملاء │ 📞 اتصل بنا │ ✉︎ راسلنا │ 📍 العنوان          │
     ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │  انضم لنشرتنا                 المتجر    المجموعات   الشركة      │
     │  سطر الوصف                    …          …           …          │
     │  [ بريدك ] ( اشترك )                                            │
     │  بالاشتراك أنت توافق على …                                      │
     │                                                                 │
     │  العربية ⌄                                      ( f )( x )( ig )│
     │  [VISA][mada][MC][…]                                            │
     ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
     │  © 2026 المتجر                        الشروط · سياسة الخصوصية   │
     └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   ── The lead column is not one of the auto-fit columns ──
   The subscribe form is a BAND across the top, not a column: it owns the full
   width above the menus, headline on one side and field on the other. It used
   to be the first cell of the link grid, where three columns beside it
   squeezed the field to 240px and wrapped the heading after two words.

   The menu grid is `repeat(var(--fo-cols), minmax(0,1fr))` plus one wider
   track for Instagram, and `--fo-cols` is the RENDERED block count printed
   once by the widget. `minmax(0,1fr)` so a sixth column shrinks the tracks
   instead of overflowing them; `--fo-ig` collapses to 0 when no Instagram
   image is set, so the row does not keep a gap for a column that is not there.

   ── The contact strip is four fixed slots, not blocks ──
   No widget in this theme declares more than one block TYPE, so a repeatable
   contact item would have to share the `column` list with the link menus — and
   the merchant could then interleave them, which the layout has no answer for.
   Four slots is also what the strip is designed for: the dividers and the
   4→2→1 grid stop making sense past four.

   ── No country / currency switcher ──
   The reference footer opens a "United States (USD $)" picker. Qumra resolves
   the market SERVER-side from `localization.market` — there is no storefront
   form that changes it, the way `{% form 'lang' %}` changes the language. A
   dropdown that cannot change anything is worse than no dropdown, so the slot
   holds the LANGUAGE switcher, which is the one thing a shopper can actually
   switch here.

   ── Payment badges ──
   Drawn marks from ui/payment-icons.njk, Gulf-first. A merchant whose provider
   requires exact trademark artwork fills `payment_image_1..3` instead, and
   those replace the drawn row rather than sitting next to it — a mixed row of
   official logos and drawn ones looks broken.

   ── RTL ──
   The whole footer flows with the document. The dividers in the contact strip
   are `border-inline-start` on every cell but the first, so they land between
   the right pairs in both directions with no override. The subscribe arrow and
   the "view all" chevrons use `.rtl-flip`.

   Styling lives in assets/style.css → "15.20 FOOTER".
   ========================================================================= #}

{# ---- External-link test, used by both menu loops below --------------------
   A merchant menu can hold anything: an internal path (/shop), an absolute URL
   back to this same store, or a link to somewhere else entirely. Only the last
   of those should leave the tab.

   `indexOf('://')` catches every absolute URL — and it is indexOf rather than
   the `in` operator because `in` is written for arrays and dicts here, and a
   string that happens to be empty or undefined makes it throw rather than
   return false. The second test lets an absolute link to THIS store stay
   in-tab, so a merchant who types their full domain out of habit does not get
   a pop-out to their own shop. `store.url` is guarded because a link must not
   become external-by-accident on a render where it is missing.

   `noopener noreferrer` matches what the social row already does. Modern
   browsers imply noopener on target="_blank", but the older ones a storefront
   still sees do not, and an explicit rel is one attribute. #}
{% macro extAttrs(url) %}{% if url and url.indexOf('://') > -1 and not (store.url and url.indexOf(store.url) == 0) %} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{% set id = widget.id %}
{% set d = widget.data %}
{% set columns = widget.blocks | default([], true) %}
{# Two columns bound to the same menu would print every link twice, and the
   default menu setting makes that the normal case. Only the first one renders. #}
{% set footCols = [] %}
{% set footSeen = [] %}
{% for block in columns %}
  {% set b = block.data %}
  {% set items = b.menu.items if b.menu and b.menu.items else b.menu %}
  {% set sig = [] %}
  {% if items %}{% for it in items %}{% set _ = sig.push(it.url or it.title) %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
  {% set sigKey = sig | join('|') %}
  {% if not (sigKey and sigKey in footSeen) %}
    {% if sigKey %}{% set _ = footSeen.push(sigKey) %}{% endif %}
    {% if b.title or sigKey %}{% set _ = footCols.push({ 'title': b.title, 'items': items if sigKey else [] }) %}{% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endfor %}


{# ---- subscribe ---- #}
{% set showNl = d.show_newsletter | default(true) %}
{% set nlAction = d.newsletter_action | default('', true) %}
{% set nlField = d.newsletter_field | default('EMAIL', true) %}
{% set nlPlaceholder = d.newsletter_placeholder | default(t('newsletter.placeholder'), true) %}
{% set nlButton = d.newsletter_button | default('', true) %}
{% set nlNote = d.newsletter_note | default('', true) %}

{# ---- store blurb ---- #}
{% set showBrand = d.show_brand | default(false) %}
{% set brandText = d.brand_text | default('', true) %}

{# ---- contact strip ---- #}
{% set showContact = d.show_contact | default(true) %}
{# A heading with no phone/e-mail/address under it says nothing — the strip
   only renders once the merchant has typed at least one contact value. #}
{% set showContact = showContact and (d.contact1_text or d.contact2_text or d.contact3_text or d.contact4_text) %}
{% set contactIconColor = d.contact_icon_color | default('', true) %}
{# The number of FILLED cells, so the grid gets `repeat(3, 1fr)` for three
   slots instead of `repeat(4, 1fr)` and a hole. Written as ONE expression on
   purpose: a running total built with `{% set %}` inside `{% if %}` blocks is
   the pattern that has bitten this theme three times, and there is no reason
   to go near it when the four slots are known. #}
{% set fcCount = (1 if d.contact1_text else 0)
               + (1 if d.contact2_text else 0)
               + (1 if d.contact3_text else 0)
               + (1 if d.contact4_text else 0) %}

{# ---- utility row ---- #}
{% set socialStyle = d.social_style | default('circle', true) %}
{% set showPay = d.show_payments | default(true) %}
{% set showLang = d.show_language_switcher | default(true) %}

{% set copyright = d.copyright | default('', true) %}
{% if not copyright %}{% set copyright = store.name | default('', true) %}{% endif %}
{% set bottomMenu = d.bottom_menu %}

{# The footer paints from its own `--color-footer-*` family, which layout.njk
   fills from the GLOBAL theme settings. `tone` swaps that whole family locally
   in the CSS — one click for the light footer the design asks for, instead of
   five colour pickers a merchant has to get consistent by hand. The pickers
   below still override whatever the tone set, so they remain the fine control.
   Empty picker = fall through, so each field doubles as its own revert.

   `--fo-bg` stays separate from `--color-footer`: the subscribe button paints
   its label with the footer's background colour and needs the picked one. #}
{# The 🎨 switch is the revert, exactly as in every other section: off and
   every pick below falls out of the <style> block entirely, so the footer
   drops straight back to `tone` and the global theme palette. The merchant's
   colours stay saved and return the moment the switch goes back on. #}
{% set colorsOn = d.colors_enabled | default(false) %}
{% set bg = (d.color_bg | default('', true)) if colorsOn else '' %}
{% set bar = (d.color_bottom_bar | default('', true)) if colorsOn else '' %}
{% set foHeading = (d.color_title | default('', true)) if colorsOn else '' %}
{% set foText = (d.color_text | default('', true)) if colorsOn else '' %}
{% set foBorder = (d.color_border | default('', true)) if colorsOn else '' %}

{% set rawLang = localization.language | default('ar', true) %}
{% set currentLang = rawLang if rawLang == 'en' else 'ar' %}

{% macro mediaUrl(m) %}{% if m %}{% if m is string %}{{ m }}{% elif m.fileUrl %}{{ m.fileUrl }}{% elif m.url %}{{ m.url }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

{% set payImg1 = mediaUrl(d.payment_image_1) | trim %}
{# Instagram tiles: three `media` slots collapsed into one list so the template
   loops once and an empty slot simply drops out. `| length`, not truthiness —
   the url macro returns a SafeString OBJECT, which is truthy even when empty. #}
{% set igRaw = [
  { 'src': mediaUrl(d.instagram_1) | trim, 'url': d.instagram_1_url },
  { 'src': mediaUrl(d.instagram_2) | trim, 'url': d.instagram_2_url },
  { 'src': mediaUrl(d.instagram_3) | trim, 'url': d.instagram_3_url }
] %}
{# Demo tiles only when the merchant has named the column (a title or handle) —
   an unnamed, unfilled column stays hidden, as before. #}
{% set igNamed = d.instagram_title or d.instagram_handle %}
{# Demo tiles only with a real account to send them to. A column of stock photos
   linking to `#` is an empty column dressed up. #}
{% set igLink = d.instagram_url or d.social_instagram %}
{% set igShots = [] %}
{% for g in igRaw %}
  {% if (g.src | length) > 0 %}{% set _ = igShots.push(g) %}
  {# HADIYA: the demo slots slot-tile-6…8 — the mosaic shows five tiles out of
     the box, so these three are free, and every preset's photos follow. #}
  {% elif igNamed and igLink %}{% set _ = igShots.push({ 'src': ('slot-tile-' ~ (loop.index + 5) ~ '.jpg') | assets, 'url': g.url }) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% set payImg2 = mediaUrl(d.payment_image_2) | trim %}
{% set payImg3 = mediaUrl(d.payment_image_3) | trim %}
{# `| length`, not truthiness — a macro returns a SafeString OBJECT, and an
   object is truthy even when it holds an empty string. #}
{% set hasPayImg = (payImg1 | length) > 0 or (payImg2 | length) > 0 or (payImg3 | length) > 0 %}


